  "summary": "Recent preprints apply LLM agents and connectors to computational chemistry runs, single-cell atlases and GEO dataset search.",
  "synthesis": "The four preprints share a design pattern in which language models are coupled to domain-specific computation or data rather than used as standalone text generators. Magnolia pairs a persistent-memory LLM agent with docking, molecular dynamics and quantum chemistry runs, using tiered memory that is human-validated. LIP instead trains connectors that map protein and small-molecule specialist embeddings into frozen LLM states for zero-shot cross-domain transfer. On the data side, GENOAR applies an agent-assisted parallel engine to organize over 54 million human and mouse single-cell transcriptomes into analysis-ready form, while GEO-BERT provides retrieval-augmented, field-aware semantic search over GEO dataset metadata. The novelty lies in persistence, frozen-model interoperability, and metadata-scale retrieval. The summaries report no quantitative results, so performance claims remain unverified.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-10-25"
}
